we're talking mainly about clouds forming

00:31:42.040 --> 00:31:43.439
within this troposphere,

00:31:43.439 --> 00:31:44.520
the lowest layer of the atmosphere,

00:31:44.520 --> 00:31:47.680
but actually you can get clouds even higher than that.

00:31:47.680 --> 00:31:50.959
So there are types of clouds called noctilucent clouds

00:31:50.959 --> 00:31:52.280
that form very high up,

00:31:52.280 --> 00:31:55.680
about 80 kilometres above the surface.

00:31:55.680 --> 00:31:59.560
It's very, very dry up in the mesosphere,

00:31:59.560 --> 00:32:00.599
but it's very, very cold.

00:32:00.599 --> 00:32:03.079
It's about minus 120 degrees Celsius there.

00:32:03.760 --> 00:32:04.719
So even though it's very dry,

00:32:04.719 --> 00:32:06.400
it gets cold enough that you can still form

00:32:06.400 --> 00:32:08.439
these very, very thin ice clouds.

00:32:08.439 --> 00:32:11.760
And you can see those sometimes if you're lucky,

00:32:11.760 --> 00:32:13.479
particularly at sort of dusk or in the morning

00:32:13.479 --> 00:32:15.439
when you get that, as Owen was describing,

00:32:15.439 --> 00:32:18.160
you get this sort of horizontal path of the light

00:32:18.160 --> 00:32:19.319
through the atmosphere,

00:32:19.319 --> 00:32:21.400
which gives you that sort of reddy colours.

00:32:21.400 --> 00:32:24.359
You can sort of see them, very like ghost-like clouds almost.

00:32:24.359 --> 00:32:25.680
Similarly, in the stratosphere,

00:32:25.680 --> 00:32:27.760
we have these mother-of-pearl clouds,

00:32:27.760 --> 00:32:29.880
they're often called, the nacreous clouds,

00:32:29.880 --> 00:32:31.640
which again form over the polar regions

00:32:31.640 --> 00:32:32.560
where it's very, very cold.

00:32:32.560 --> 00:32:34.920
And again, you can get these beautiful effects,

00:32:34.920 --> 00:32:37.359
like light effects, if you're lucky enough to see those.

