and I remember this thing, my father going out

00:40:04.120 --> 00:40:05.719
and sort of saying to my older brother,

00:40:05.719 --> 00:40:08.879
oh, this thing's in the garden, and I was tiny,

00:40:08.879 --> 00:40:11.399
but I can remember this weather balloon in the garden,

00:40:11.399 --> 00:40:13.560
and it looked like a big polystyrene box

00:40:13.560 --> 00:40:16.120
with some sort of material attached to it,

00:40:16.120 --> 00:40:19.199
and apparently I went up to it and I gave it a good kick,

00:40:19.199 --> 00:40:22.320
and that was my introduction to weather forecasting,

00:40:22.320 --> 00:40:24.840
I think, and all these years later,

00:40:24.840 --> 00:40:27.320
